{"id":"s4.1.2","slug":"multiplying-three-digit-by-three-digit","title":"Multiplying Three-Digit Number by Three-Digit Number","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">This is an extension of the previous section and the procedure is the same but requires a little more multiplication and bookkeeping. Let $n_1 = abc$ and $n_2 = def$, where a, b, c, d, e, f are digits. You’ll want to do the groups of $n_1$ as $a$ and $bc$ and $n_2$ as $d$ and $ef$ and perform the FOIL/LOIFing.</p><p>$abc = 100a + (bc)$ and $def = 100d + (ef)$</p><p>$[100a + (bc)] \\times [100d + (ef)] = 10000ad + 100[a(ef) + d(bc)] + (bc)(ef)$</p><p>This shows us that:</p><ol class=\"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li>Again, the ones and tens digit of the answer is simply the last two digits when performing the multiplication of the groups of bc and ef.</li><li>Again, carries are common, so keep track!</li></ol>","summary":"This is an extension of the previous section and the procedure is the same but requires a little more multiplication and bookkeeping.","generation_guideline":"Generate a multiplication problem of two 3-digit numbers.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $212 \\times 311$.","answer":"65932","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $208^2$.","answer":"43264","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $404^2$.","answer":"163216","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $331 \\times 122$.","answer":"40382","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $707^2$.","answer":"499849","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $131 \\times 223$.","answer":"29213","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $402^2$.","answer":"161604","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate $804^2$.","answer":"646416","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":9,"text":"Calculate $234 \\times 211$.","answer":"49374","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":10,"tex